WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.181 --> 00:00:21.938
"I can't believe you're going to be on TV, Ben," Gaby said on the way home from school.

2
00:00:21.939 --> 00:00:24.014
"You'll be famous!"

3
00:00:24.015 --> 00:00:27.319
Ben frowned. "I don't want to be famous.

4
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.431
I don't even want to be on Kids' Kitchen Showdown."

5
00:00:31.432 --> 00:00:39.561
After Mr. Icky had picked Ben to be on the TV show, everyone was excited.

6
00:00:39.562 --> 00:00:44.364
Winnie had given Ben a big hug. "You'll do great!"

7
00:00:44.365 --> 00:00:48.836
Other monsters patted him on the back and gave him the claws-up sign.

8
00:00:48.837 --> 00:00:53.486
Some monsters even looked a bit jealous.

9
00:00:53.487 --> 00:00:57.163
Gaby was still talking as she and Ben walked along.

10
00:00:57.164 --> 00:00:59.792
"I didn't even know you liked cooking."

11
00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:04.604
"I hate cooking," Ben said. "Mr. Icky made a mistake.

12
00:01:04.605 --> 00:01:07.269
I accidentally made something that tastes good.

13
00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:10.372
But that doesn't mean I know what I'm doing."

14
00:01:10.373 --> 00:01:13.019
"You're being silly," Gaby said.

15
00:01:13.019 --> 00:01:17.020
"You obviously have talent and don't realize it."

16
00:01:17.021 --> 00:01:20.993
"Well, I'm not going to win the competition," Ben went on.

17
00:01:20.994 --> 00:01:22.586
"The judges are humans.

18
00:01:22.587 --> 00:01:31.434
They're going to choose a human cook—not a monster."

19
00:01:31.435 --> 00:01:38.536
That evening Ben sat on his back stoop, trying to distract himself from the cooking show.

20
00:01:38.537 --> 00:01:42.767
He made himself think about possible birthday presents for Winnie.

21
00:01:42.768 --> 00:01:46.662
"What do witches like?" he asked himself.

22
00:01:46.663 --> 00:01:49.261
He thought about Winnie's favorite things.

23
00:01:49.262 --> 00:01:55.077
She loved to fly. Maybe she'd like a new broom?

24
00:01:55.078 --> 00:01:58.334
Ben pulled out his phone.

25
00:01:58.335 --> 00:02:02.161
He found a website that sold flying brooms.

26
00:02:02.162 --> 00:02:05.310
One broom was shaped like a lightning bolt.

27
00:02:05.311 --> 00:02:08.338
Ben watched a demonstration video.

28
00:02:08.339 --> 00:02:14.003
The broom was so fast, it left a streak of fire across the sky.

29
00:02:14.004 --> 00:02:20.807
"Wow!" Ben said. "Winnie would love this broom. How much does it cost?"

30
00:02:20.808 --> 00:02:25.190
He scrolled down the page and found the price.

31
00:02:25.191 --> 00:02:29.717
"Six thousand dollars?" Ben gulped.

32
00:02:29.718 --> 00:02:32.963
There was no way he could afford that.

33
00:02:32.964 --> 00:02:36.100
He looked at some other flying broom websites.

34
00:02:36.101 --> 00:02:39.742
The cheapest broom Ben saw was still too expensive.

35
00:02:39.743 --> 00:02:44.801
It was five hundred dollars, and it looked like a piece of junk.

36
00:02:44.802 --> 00:02:49.531
Ben's shoulders slumped, and he put his phone away.

37
00:02:49.532 --> 00:02:55.611
As Ben brooded, the hedge that ran down the side of his yard shook slightly.

38
00:02:55.612 --> 00:03:00.340
Something was rustling on the ground.

39
00:03:00.341 --> 00:03:03.109
Ben peered over.

40
00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:08.385
"Who's there?" he said. There was no answer.

41
00:03:08.386 --> 00:03:11.344
For a moment the hedge was still.

42
00:03:11.345 --> 00:03:13.816
Then it moved again.

43
00:03:13.817 --> 00:03:17.728
"Something is in there," Ben thought.

44
00:03:17.729 --> 00:03:22.216
He floated over for a closer look.

45
00:03:22.217 --> 00:03:27.446
He moved some of the leaves out of the way and looked in at the branches.

46
00:03:27.447 --> 00:03:30.919
A pair of glowing eyes stared back at him.

47
00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:36.496
A chill ran down Ben's spine. "It's a . . . a kitten!"

48
00:03:36.497 --> 00:03:42.245
Meow! The tiny black kitten leaped out of the hedge and straight toward Ben.

49
00:03:42.246 --> 00:03:43.851
Ben jumped to the side.

50
00:03:43.852 --> 00:03:46.047
The kitten landed on the grass.

51
00:03:46.048 --> 00:03:49.209
It looked up at Ben and hissed.

52
00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:52.998
"Oh, boy," Ben said, glancing around.

53
00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:56.550
A lot of monsters and humans loved cats.

54
00:03:56.551 --> 00:03:59.870
But cats hated ghosts!

55
00:03:59.871 --> 00:04:04.379
Ben ran toward his back door with the kitten chasing him all the way.

56
00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:09.522
"Mom will be furious if this beast gets inside," Ben thought.

57
00:04:09.523 --> 00:04:12.182
He shot across his backyard.

58
00:04:12.183 --> 00:04:17.217
The kitten sprinted behind him, hissing and pouncing at his feet.

59
00:04:17.218 --> 00:04:21.070
Ben floated through his fence and into a neighbor's backyard.

60
00:04:21.071 --> 00:04:23.279
He stopped to catch his breath.

61
00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:25.648
"Whew! I think I lost—"

62
00:04:25.649 --> 00:04:29.705
Hiss! Meow! The kitten was on top of the fence.

63
00:04:29.706 --> 00:04:32.537
It leaped down and fell right through Ben.

64
00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:37.942
"Ahh!" Ben dashed through the neighbor's yard and onto the street.

65
00:04:37.943 --> 00:04:40.671
The kitten was still right behind him.

66
00:04:40.672 --> 00:04:44.023
Ben darted upward, flying over the trees.

67
00:04:44.024 --> 00:04:46.595
Looking down, he saw the kitten.

68
00:04:46.596 --> 00:04:51.436
It was still hissing at him, but at least it couldn't fly.

69
00:04:51.437 --> 00:05:00.491
With a sigh of relief, Ben flew home.

70
00:05:00.492 --> 00:05:07.030
On Wednesday morning Ben was one of the first students to arrive in the cooking classroom.

71
00:05:07.031 --> 00:05:14.267
He saw Mr. Icky pulling pots from one of the cabinets.

72
00:05:14.268 --> 00:05:19.642
"Um, Mr. Icky," Ben said. "Can I talk to you for a second?"

73
00:05:19.643 --> 00:05:22.167
Mr. Icky turned around.

74
00:05:22.168 --> 00:05:27.129
"Ah, Ben, my master monster chef! What do you need?"

75
00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:29.657
Ben put down his books.

76
00:05:29.658 --> 00:05:33.719
"I don't think I should be on Kids' Kitchen Showdown."

77
00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:38.810
"What?" Mr. Icky peered closely at Ben.

78
00:05:38.811 --> 00:05:40.721
"I'm not really good at cooking.

79
00:05:40.722 --> 00:05:43.111
I make mistakes all the time.

80
00:05:43.112 --> 00:05:47.688
If my food turns out well, it's totally by accident."

81
00:05:47.689 --> 00:05:51.136
"Nonsense," Mr. Icky said.

82
00:05:51.137 --> 00:05:53.450
"You have a natural talent, Ben.

83
00:05:53.451 --> 00:05:57.003
And I've already given your name to Mr. Freaky."

84
00:05:57.004 --> 00:06:01.222
By now other students were entering the classroom.

85
00:06:01.223 --> 00:06:03.988
"Good morning, everyone," the teacher called.

86
00:06:03.989 --> 00:06:08.011
"Let's get started."

87
00:06:08.012 --> 00:06:14.208
After Mr. Icky described the morning's assignment, Mog came over to Ben.

88
00:06:14.209 --> 00:06:18.495
"Hey, Ben," Mog said. "I heard you talking to Mr. Icky.

89
00:06:18.496 --> 00:06:21.648
I know how you can get out of doing the show."

90
00:06:21.649 --> 00:06:24.287
"You do?" Ben was doubtful.

91
00:06:24.288 --> 00:06:28.992
Mog was a good friend, but he didn't usually have smart ideas.

92
00:06:28.993 --> 00:06:35.215
Mog leaned in closer. "Cook badly today!"
